        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "A Tale of Three Intersecting Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.085,
            0.293,
            0.109
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.112,
            0.847,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "1. Construct triangles for the following measurements where the angle is included between the sides:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.155,
            0.409,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": "(a) 3 cm, 75°, 7 cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.178,
            0.409,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "(b) 6 cm, 25°, 3 cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.202,
            0.419,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": "(c) 3 cm, $1 2 0 ^ { \\circ } ,$ 8 cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.232,
            0.838,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "? We have seen that triangles do not exist for all sets of sidelengths. Is there a combination of measurements in the case of two sides M and the included angle where a triangle is not possible? Justify T your answer using what you observe during construction."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.809,
            0.252,
            0.896,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.337,
            0.568,
            0.359
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Two Angles and the Included Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.369,
            0.849,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "In this case, we are given two angles and the side that is a part of both angles, which we call the included side. Here are some examples of such measurements:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.428,
            0.843,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.591,
            0.8,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": "Construct a triangle ABC where $\\mathrm { A B } = 5$ cm, $\\angle \\mathrm{A} = 45^{\\circ}$ and $\\angle \\mathrm{B} = 80^{\\circ}$ Let us take the given side as the base."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.652,
            0.594,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.764,
            0.557,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1:** Draw the base AB of length 5 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.783,
            0.617,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": "**Step 2:** Draw $\\angle \\mathrm { A }$ and $\\angle \\mathrm { B }$ of measures $4 5 ^ { \\circ } ;$ , and $8 0 ^ { \\circ }$ respectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.819,
            0.617,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "**Step 3:** The point of intersection of the two new line segments is the third vertex C."
